OL,3,GNEWSAMore NI bee colonies survived
OL,4,Awinter last year
OL,5,
OL,6,FFewer bee colonies were lost last
OL,7,Fwinter in Northern Ireland, new figures
OL,8,Fshow.
OL,10,FThe annual honey bee husbandry survey
OL,11,Fby the Agri-Food and Biosciences
OL,12,FInstitute (AFBI) found about
OL,13,Fone-in-four colonies were lost in
OL,14,F2025/26, compared to a third in
OL,15,F2024/25.
OL,17,FAbout half (51%) the losses were linked
OL,18,Fto problems with the queen bee. Others
OL,19,Fwere lost because bees were dead or the
OL,20,Fhive was empty. Natural hazards
OL,21,Fincluding storms, flood and theft
OL,22,Faccounted for 10%.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
